     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br>I am just starting to use biogeoBEARS. I wanted to know if the geography file can be a csv file with two columns having the tip names and tip ranges ? Something like this<br><br>\r\n <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"148\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:48pt\" width=\"64\">\r\n <col style=\"width:63pt\" width=\"84\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt;width:48pt\" height=\"20\" width=\"64\">Aleuro<span>    </span></td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:63pt\" width=\"84\"> 00001000000</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">017 Euble<span> </span></td>\r\n  <td> 00010000000</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">181 E satp</td>\r\n  <td> 00000000100</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">015 Euble<span> </span></td>\r\n  <td> 00000000100</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15.0pt\" height=\"20\">172 E satp</td>\r\n  <td> 00000000100</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table><br></div>"
